{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-IMPLEMENTATION TRIAGE OF ITEM 3 (validate_assignee_exists): IT IS A PURE TEST GAP, NOT A\nLATENT PRODUCT BUG. The plan says 'if any path returns a bool or an accountId-shaped value, a bug is\nfiled' — checked at df41edcf25 so the implementer does not have to hold that possibility open.\n\nadapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:704 declares '-> str' and has exactly TWO exits:\n  * return str(_user_attr(user, \"name\") or assignee)   <- a DC USERNAME string\n  * raise AssigneeNotFoundError(...)                     <- the documented miss\nNo path returns a bool, and none returns an accountId-shaped value. The docstring already states the\nreturn contract in the same terms the ticket does, including why returning True or an accountId\nwould corrupt the identity, and why the error type must be AssigneeNotFoundError SPECIFICALLY\n(outbound_assignee branches on type(exc).__name__, so any other type — a NotImplementedError in\nparticular — would silently and permanently downgrade every DC assignee resolution to the\nnon-authoritative string-match fallback).\n\nSO: the contract is implemented and documented; what is missing is any ASSERTION of it. That is\nexactly the ticket's characterisation — 'a real gap wearing a test's clothes' — and it means item 3\nneeds a test written, and NO bug ticket filed. The implementer should still check the CLOUD side\n(adapters/jira/acli.py:541) independently rather than inferring parity from this, since the AC asks\nfor the return value to be asserted for BOTH backends and Cloud's contract is deliberately\ndifferent (accountId, not name).\n\nNote the mutation check for this item has to bite on the RETURN VALUE, not on presence: the existing\nvacuous assertion is 'assert hasattr(cls, \"validate_assignee_exists\")', which the parametrized\npresence test in the same file already makes verbatim, so a rewrite that still only proves existence\nwould reproduce the defect this ticket exists to remove."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785690588006074001,"uuid":"c4f30878-0db7-4f6c-bce8-626bc144f637"}